For the \texttt{CartPole}, the maximum reward is always when balancing the pole and the regularization has little effect.
For the \texttt{MountainCar}, the agent obtains the maximum reward on top of the mountain. But, the reward landscape is much more well-behaved when the environment has textures and we add goal-baseline regularization -- this is consistent with our results when training policies.}
